{#
  A person's picture cropped to head and shoulders.

  Anchoring on a focal point (img-pos.twig) moves the frame; it cannot make it
  smaller. A full-length photograph in a portrait box still shows the whole
  person, waist and all, only moved (Cameron Smyth, 29 September 2026). So an
  image listed in _data/portrait-crops.json is drawn larger than its box, by
  that image's own zoom, and placed so its focal point sits centred across and
  a third of the way down, never showing past the photograph's own edges. The
  zoom is per image because the need is: a painted bust needs none, a standing
  figure in a landscape frame nearly three times.

  An image not listed is drawn as before: object-fit cover, anchored on its
  focal point where it has one, else the top.

  Params
    img    the asset, or null
    ratio  the box's height over its width: 4/3 for a 3:4 card, 5/4 for the
           4:5 record portrait, 1 for the round thumbnails
    alt    alt text
    fill   true when the parent already has a fixed size (cards, thumbnails);
           false to give the box its own aspect ratio (the record portrait)
#}
{% macro img(img, ratio, alt, fill, w) %}
  {#- w: optional width in pixels to resize to, for cards that never need the original (the war memorial's wall). -#}
  {%- set src = (w ?? null) and img and img.width and img.width > w ? img.getUrl({ width: w, mode: 'fit' }) : (img ? img.url : '') -%}
  {%- if img -%}
    {%- set crops = source('_data/portrait-crops.json', ignore_missing = true)|json_decode -%}
    {%- set crop = crops ? (crops[img.id ~ ''] ?? null) : null -%}
    {%- if crop and img.width and img.height and img.getHasFocalPoint() -%}
      {%- set fp = img.getFocalPoint() -%}
      {%- set a = img.width / img.height -%}
      {%- set h = ratio -%}
      {%- set z = crop.zoom -%}
      {#- The image covering the box at zoom 1, in units of the box's width. -#}
      {%- set rw = max(1, h * a) * z -%}
      {%- set rh = rw / a -%}
      {%- set left = min(0, max(1 - rw, 0.5 - fp.x * rw)) -%}
      {%- set top = min(0, max(h - rh, h * 0.34 - fp.y * rh)) -%}
      <span class="pcrop" style="display:block;position:relative;overflow:hidden;width:100%;{{ fill ? 'height:100%' : 'aspect-ratio:1/' ~ h }}"><img src="{{ src }}" alt="{{ alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="position:absolute;max-width:none;height:auto;aspect-ratio:auto;object-fit:fill;width:{{ (rw * 100)|round(2) }}%;left:{{ (left * 100)|round(2) }}%;top:{{ (top / h * 100)|round(2) }}%"></span>
    {%- else -%}
      <img src="{{ src }}" alt="{{ alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"{% include '_partials/record/img-pos.twig' with {img: img} only %}>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
